identifier: ExoInstruments
$kref: '#/ckan/github/batistitooo/ExoInstruments'
$vref: '#/ckan/ksp-avc'
license: restricted
author: batistitooo
abstract: >-
  An observational astronomy mod: real telescopes photographing planets, moons,
  nebulae and galaxies onto real detector models, plus an exoplanet survey with
  transit and radial-velocity pipelines against a real star catalog.
description: >-
  Adds a working observatory to KSP, alongside the stock science system rather
  than in place of it. Photograph anything in the sky, from moons to galaxies,
  through real named telescopes (a PlaneWave astrograph, the VLT, a launchable
  space telescope) onto real detector models, and get FITS files that calibrate
  and stack in real astronomy software. Or run an actual exoplanet survey:
  select a real star from an exoplanet.eu-derived catalog, choose an instrument
  suited to its brightness and detection method, and extract a signal from
  simulated, photon-noise-limited data. Includes transit timing variations
  (TTV), the Rossiter-McLaughlin effect, and a career-mode
  instrument-acquisition economy. Everything works out of the box; the optional
  sky data (Gaia star field, dust, galaxies and their images) is downloaded by
  tools/get_sky_data_compact.py or tools/get_sky_data_complete.py, and is not
  required.
resources:
  homepage: https://github.com/batistitooo/ExoInstruments
  repository: https://github.com/batistitooo/ExoInstruments
  license: https://github.com/batistitooo/ExoInstruments/blob/main/LICENSE
tags:
  - science
  - physics
recommends:
  - name: BetterTimeWarpCont
  - name: EnvironmentalVisualEnhancements
suggests:
  - name: Spectra
install:
  - file: GameData/ExoInstruments
    install_to: GameData
